# Temporary tests — delete after use

When you write a test file under `tests/` (or elsewhere) only to verify a fix in this chat:

1. Run it once if needed.
2. **Delete the test file immediately after** — do not leave it in the repo.
3. Do not commit those ad-hoc test files.
4. Prefer fixing code and confirming via existing behavior / manual check when enough; avoid creating permanent test files unless the user explicitly asks to keep a test suite.

Existing long-lived tests already in the project stay until the user asks to remove them.
